{
  "description": "Pathological value trees for the shared walker (#11). Each case names a shape that both languages build from the same parameters, instead of storing multi-megabyte JSON. Every case asserts that the walk terminates, never passes the planted synthetic secret through, and calls the scanner no more often than the named limit allows. `maxScannerCalls` is an upper bound, not an expected count. A `cause-chain` is an error whose cause is an error, `depth` levels deep, with the leaf only in the innermost message. A `shared-reference` is `{x: s, y: s}` for one non-cyclic `s = {leaf}`. Optional: `mustNotContain`, a string the serialized result must not contain, and `expected`, the exact result. An `opaque-object` is a class instance holding the leaf in an attribute and in its string form; TS walks it as its own properties, Python fails closed to `[REDACTED:ERROR]` (#85), so its `mustContain` names each language's result. A `throwing-entry` is a mapping whose `bad` entry raises when read and whose `ok` entry is the leaf. Python serializes with `default=str`, like a JSON log formatter. Limits may be deliberately invalid (null, negative, a string, a boolean): both languages fall back to the default.",
